    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **46 tests, 0 failures**, including the new Cp33 future-date test.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: reject a create-owner request whose supplied `registrationDate` is later than the server date, responding **400**. Following this project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not `@RestController`/`@ControllerAdvice`), I added a rejection step + escalation handler:\n\n1. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** (function step) \u2014 reads the published `OwnerFieldsDto`; if `getRegistrationDate()` is non-null and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, throws the checked exception. A request with no supplied date (defaults to today) is always allowed.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and routes to escalation).\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing handler style (reusing `ProblemDetails.build`).\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** `.../escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` right after `validate` and before `resolveRegistrationDate`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nPlacement matters: the check runs on the **raw supplied date** *before* `ResolveRegistrationDate` applies weekend roll-forward, so it's the supplied value that's compared against the server date \u2014 exactly what the spec asks. The existing weekend-rollover behavior (Cp07/Cp20) is untouched.",
